{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/940368-the-venture-brothers-in-the-world-of-darkness","id":940368,"title":"The Venture Brothers in the World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-30T18:19:09-07:00","id":940368,"title":"The Venture Brothers in the World of Darkness","content":"I was wondering how everyone would create the Venture Brothers in the World of Darkness. I think that the majority of superscientists could be represented as sorcerers using Scientific Numina, but the superheroes like Captain Sunshine are a bit difficult (though they may be modeled as fomori from Possessed or consors out of Ascension's Right Hand). Dr. Orpheus would be created as a sorcerer practicing Mythic Numina (though he may be a really lame Mage instead).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T18:34:30-07:00","id":940375,"title":"","content":"This would all fall into the Sons of Ether in Mage. All this super-science stuff falls under that. Dr Jonas Ventrue was obviously a real Mage. His son, Doc Venture is a really inept Son of Ether. Maybe one Arete, but he has all these devices left over from his father. Most of the other characters would be various types of consors, some of whom are also supernatural (such as the Order of the Triad members). Most of the outright superheroes couldn't be used as they'd lead to massive Paradox, but it is possible there is some umbral plane out there where they do their actual superheroics. You'd need to make a lot of changes to adapt it into the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T19:44:43-07:00","id":940397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/940368-the-venture-brothers-in-the-world-of-darkness#post940368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering how everyone would create the Venture Brothers in the World of Darkness. I think that the majority of superscientists could be represented as sorcerers using Scientific Numina, but the superheroes like Captain Sunshine are a bit difficult (though they may be modeled as fomori from Possessed or consors out of Ascension's Right Hand). Dr. Orpheus would be created as a sorcerer practicing Mythic Numina (though he may be a really lame Mage instead).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you want a World of Darkness that looks outwardly like the Venture Brothers? A world where captain Sunshine exists.. and the city is Run by a Ventrue Prince? If that's the case I believe there's Rules for a more legitimate crossover in teh Mage ST handbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T20:08:25-07:00","id":940409,"title":"","content":"It is more that I am curious about how people would represent the various characters than anything else. I do not think that most of the super scientists are Mages because they require too much time in the creation of their gadgets. I think that the majority of their gadgets could be explained with very high levels of Advanced Chemistry Procedures (Alchemy) and Advanced Engineering Procedures. The ray shield that Dr. Venture created for Gargantua II took months and hundreds of interns to create and, quite frankly, resulted in massive genetic mutations that transformed most of the intern into monsters. I do not think that would be True Magick because it takes too long and has too many strange side effects.<br /> <br /> Could you not create Captain Sunshine by using the rules in Possessed or the rules in Ascension's Right Hand. While he might not seem to be a fomori, there is a running theme of inappropriate relationships between Captain Sunshine and Wonder Boy. Neither option creates Paradox and, quite frankly, Captain Sunshine did not seem to have a Mage's flexibility (he could fly, cause painful sunburns, and had super strength, but he did not seem to do much else).<br /> <br /> I do not think that the public super science would work in the WoD, but I can imagine that secret super science would be quite feasible (since that is what the Technocracy is all about). The flying cocoons and other stuff could be given camouflage and stealth systems, so the normal people would not notice them. Or you could have something similar to the Possessed power of Memory Caress, where people forget or rationalize what they have seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T20:19:48-07:00","id":940413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/940368-the-venture-brothers-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=940397#post940397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do you want a World of Darkness that looks outwardly like the Venture Brothers? A world where captain Sunshine exists.. and the city is Run by a Ventrue Prince? If that's the case I believe there's Rules for a more legitimate crossover in teh Mage ST handbook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, the board a few notches up, regarding the Aeon Continuum, is a much easier fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T21:02:10-07:00","id":940432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/940368-the-venture-brothers-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=940409#post940409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is more that I am curious about how people would represent the various characters than anything else. I do not think that most of the super scientists are Mages because they require too much time in the creation of their gadgets. I think that the majority of their gadgets could be explained with very high levels of Advanced Chemistry Procedures (Alchemy) and Advanced Engineering Procedures. The ray shield that Dr. Venture created for Gargantua II took months and hundreds of interns to create and, quite frankly, resulted in massive genetic mutations that transformed most of the intern into monsters. I do not think that would be True Magick because it takes too long and has too many strange side effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>How long do you think WOnders take to make? Taking months or years to build an appropriate wonder is par for the course especially for something so large. I mean look at the VE book for how long it takes to build parts for a Voidship and that's straight up what ti was. As for Strange Side effects that is straight up a flaw built into Wonders or it could be a paradox effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could you not create Captain Sunshine by using the rules in Possessed or the rules in Ascension's Right Hand. While he might not seem to be a fomori, there is a running theme of inappropriate relationships between Captain Sunshine and Wonder Boy. Neither option creates Paradox and, quite frankly, Captain Sunshine did not seem to have a Mage's flexibility (he could fly, cause painful sunburns, and had super strength, but he did not seem to do much else). </div> </div> </div>Ascension's right hand, Or just build him with Blessings from the base Mage book. Or make him a SIdhe or a KJ.. some guy who can fly and blast you with energy and is super strong isn't exactly a hard build for the World of Darkness. He could be a Low torment Demon. Or an actual spirit(Umbra 20 has Super hero spirits in them)/<br /> <br /> The issue is more his publicity. If you just want someone with the powers.. well you have alot of options.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not think that the public super science would work in the WoD, but I can imagine that secret super science would be quite feasible (since that is what the Technocracy is all about). The flying cocoons and other stuff could be given camouflage and stealth systems, so the normal people would not notice them. Or you could have something similar to the Possessed power of Memory Caress, where people forget or rationalize what they have seen. </div> </div> </div>The Level of Publicity is what makes the Venture brothers setting what it is. You could easily put a World of darkness beneath its exterior or you can take inspiration and move it into the world of Darkness as its standard.<br /> <br /> You just have to pick your pieces. Jonas couldn't be as forward and outgoing with his tech as it shows. He may have been able to describe his adventures via comic and tv series but its probably under a psuedonym so nothing as obvious as the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/940368-the-venture-brothers-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=940413#post940413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ultimately, the board a few notches up, regarding the Aeon Continuum, is a much easier fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many Roads lead to the mountain top.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T21:04:26-07:00","id":940434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/940368-the-venture-brothers-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=940432#post940432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Many Roads lead to the mountain top.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not <i>the</i> mountain top. <i>A</i> mountain top. No guarantee that it's the one you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist